 "narr": {
  "Aqua Shard": "Aqua Shard drew 25,710 users in W26, 22% below the same FY week last year, with conversion at 5.53% versus 5.85% LY, so GA4 bookings landed at 1423 against 1933 a year ago. Google ran £5,570 for 413 bookings; Meta held 168 schedules at £18.0.",
  "Hutong": "Hutong drew 14,461 users in W26, 5% below the same FY week last year, with conversion at 5.48% versus 6.45% LY, so GA4 bookings landed at 792 against 985 a year ago. Google ran £1,380 for 287 bookings; Meta held 211 schedules at £10.15.",
  "Regent St": "Regent St drew 6,159 users in W26, 17% below the same FY week last year, with conversion at 4.58% versus 4.11% LY, so GA4 bookings landed at 282 against 303 a year ago. Google ran £702 for 55 bookings; Meta held 67 schedules at £15.25.",
  "Azzurra": "Azzurra drew 1,617 users in W26, 28% below the same FY week last year, with conversion at 4.7% versus 3.89% LY, so GA4 bookings landed at 76 against 87 a year ago. Google ran £641 for 15 bookings; Meta held 40 schedules at £14.17.",
  "Shiro Sushi": "Shiro Sushi drew 1,359 users in W26, 40% below the same FY week last year, with conversion at 10.6% versus 4.81% LY, so GA4 bookings landed at 144 against 109 a year ago. Google ran £727 for 93 bookings; Meta held 40 schedules at £7.85.",
  "DSL": "DSL (Dim Sum Library) leads the portfolio on conversion at 9.57% on 5,478 users, with GA4 bookings of 524. NOTE: DSL rebranded, so the 2025 lines are pre-rebrand (Luci) and are NOT a like-for-like comparison — the apparent YoY gains are a rebrand artefact and last year's Google data does not exist on this account."
